so complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered service/data behavior. Hygiene is good apart from minor retained diagnostic and backup residue.","limitations":["The fixed after-executor node1 listening-socket snapshot is empty, which conflicts with the shortly preceding direct `ss` observation and successful post-reboot client reads. The stronger task-specific evidence supports success, but final listener continuity is not perfectly corroborated.","Failed-service collection was unsupported on this legacy non-systemd platform, so broad service-health verification is unavailable.","The apparent retained `/etc/default/rsync.benchmark-backup` follows from the complete command trace but was not independently inventoried in the final lifecycle snapshot."]}
